      "order": 1,
      "title": "Memory coalescing",
      "objective": "Map threads to addresses so each warp issues full 128-byte transactions; reason about bandwidth-bound kernels.",
      "interview_tip": "Open with bytes moved vs. peak bandwidth: if you are far from peak in an elementwise kernel, check access patterns before anything else.",
